<body>
<div class="container">

<header>
    <h1>Active Satellites in Earth Orbit — 2026 Catalog Analysis</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">CelesTrak / NORAD TLE-based catalog &bull; 14,875 active satellites &bull; Data as of March 2026</p>
</header>

<div class="highlight-box">
    <strong>Key Finding:</strong> SpaceX's Starlink constellation comprises <strong>10,083 satellites</strong> — 67.8% of all active satellites — dwarfing all other operators combined. Launch activity has accelerated dramatically: 90.5% of the active fleet was launched since 2020.
</div>

<!-- KPI Summary -->
<div class="kpi-grid">
    <div class="kpi-card">
        <div class="kpi-label">Total Active Satellites</div>
        <div class="kpi-value">14,875</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
        <div class="kpi-label">LEO Share (MEAN_MOTION &gt; 14)</div>
        <div class="kpi-value">86.5%</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
        <div class="kpi-label">Starlink Constellation Size</div>
        <div class="kpi-value highlight">10,083</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
        <div class="kpi-label">Median Inclination</div>
        <div class="kpi-value">53.16°</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
        <div class="kpi-label">Launched Since 2020</div>
        <div class="kpi-value">13,461</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
        <div class="kpi-label">Non-Starlink Satellites</div>
        <div class="kpi-value">4,792</div>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- SECTION 1: Catalog Overview -->
<div class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">1. Catalog Overview & Key Figures</h2>
    <div class="two-col">
        <div>
            <div class="stat-row"><span class="stat-label">Total Satellites</span><span class="stat-value">14,875</span></div>
            <div class="stat-row"><span class="stat-label">Catalog Epoch Range</span><span class="stat-value">Feb 26 – Mar 30, 2026</span></div>
            <div class="stat-row"><span class="stat-label">Mean Motion Range</span><span class="stat-value">0.283 – 16.30 rev/day</span></div>
            <div class="stat-row"><span class="stat-label">Inclination Range</span><span class="stat-value">0° – 150°</span></div>
            <div class="stat-row"><span class="stat-label">High Eccentricity Orbits (e &gt; 0.1)</span><span class="stat-value">41</span></div>
            <div class="stat-row"><span class="stat-label">Unclassified (U)</span><span class="stat-value">100%</span></div>
        </div>
        <div>
            <p style="color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:0.75rem;">The active satellite population spans a wide range of orbital regimes, from low-drag LEO to GEO. The catalog is current as of late March 2026, reflecting the latest TLE epoch data from NORAD/CelesTrak.</p>
            <p style="color:var(--text-secondary);">Starlink satellites dominate, with only ~4,800 non-Starlink active satellites in the entire catalog.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- SECTION 2: Orbital Regime Classification -->
<div class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">2. Orbital Regime Classification</h2>
    <p style="color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:1rem;">
        Classification based on <strong>MEAN_MOTION thresholds</strong>: LEO &gt; 14 rev/day; MEO 1.0–14 rev/day; GEO 0.99–1.01 rev/day; HEO = remaining orbits with MEAN_MOTION &lt; 0.99 or unusual parameters.
    </p>
    <div class="regime-bar">
        <div class="regime-segment" style="flex:86.45;background:#38bdf8;color:#0f172a;">86.5%</div>
        <div class="regime-segment" style="flex:9.49;background:#4ade80;color:#0f172a;">9.5%</div>
        <div class="regime-segment" style="flex:3.93;background:#fb923c;color:#0f172a;">3.9%</div>
        <div class="regime-segment" style="flex:0.13;background:#c084fc;color:#0f172a;">0.1%</div>
    </div>
    <div class="regime-legend">
        <div class="legend-item"><div class="legend-dot" style="background:#38bdf8;"></div>LEO (12,860)</div>
        <div class="legend-item"><div class="legend-dot" style="background:#4ade80;"></div>MEO (1,412)</div>
        <div class="legend-item"><div class="legend-dot" style="background:#fb923c;"></div>GEO (584)</div>
        <div class="legend-item"><div class="legend-dot" style="background:#c084fc;"></div>HEO (19)</div>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Regime</th><th>Threshold</th><th>Count</th><th>Share</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><strong>LEO</strong></td><td>MEAN_MOTION &gt; 14 rev/day</td><td class="number">12,860</td><td class="number">86.45%</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>MEO</strong></td><td>1.0 &lt; MEAN_MOTION ≤ 14</td><td class="number">1,412</td><td class="number">9.49%</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>GEO</strong></td><td>0.99 ≤ MEAN_MOTION ≤ 1.01</td><td class="number">584</td><td class="number">3.93%</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>HEO</strong></td><td>MEAN_MOTION &lt; 0.99 or unusual</td><td class="number">19</td><td class="number">0.13%</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- SECTION 3: Constellation & Operator Breakdown -->
<div class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">3. Major Constellation & Operator Breakdown</h2>
    <div class="two-col">
        <div>
            <div class="chart-container">
                <canvas id="constellationChart"></canvas>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div>
            <table>
                <thead><tr><th>Constellation / Operator</th><th class="number">Count</th><th class="number">Share</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr style="background:rgba(56,189,248,0.1);"><td><strong>Starlink (SpaceX)</strong></td><td class="number">10,083</td><td class="number">67.8%</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>OneWeb</td><td class="number">651</td><td class="number">4.4%</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Cosmos (Russian Fed.)</td><td class="number">126</td><td class="number">0.8%</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Iridium</td><td class="number">80</td><td class="number">0.5%</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>BeiDou</td><td class="number">55</td><td class="number">0.4%</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Intelsat</td><td class="number">28</td><td class="number">0.2%</td></tr>
                    <tr><td> SES</td><td class="number">20</td><td class="number">0.1%</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Orbcomm</td><td class="number">15</td><td class="number">0.1%</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>ISS (all modules)</td><td class="number">10</td><td class="number">0.07%</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Amazon (Kuiper)</td><td class="number">6</td><td class="number">0.04%</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Swarm</td><td class="number">3</td><td class="number">0.02%</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Hubble</td><td class="number">2</td><td class="number">0.01%</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
            <p class="note">"Cosmos" entries include various Russian government/military satellites across multiple orbital regimes.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="takeaway">
        <strong>Constellation dominance:</strong> Starlink alone accounts for 67.8% of all active satellites. Excluding Starlink, the remaining 4,792 satellites represent a diverse but fragmented population of government, commercial, and scientific assets.
    </div>
</div>

<!-- SECTION 4: Launch Year Trends -->
<div class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">4. Launch Year Trends</h2>
    <p style="color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:1rem;">Historical growth of the active satellite fleet, derived from OBJECT_ID launch-year prefix. The chart reveals the dramatic acceleration in launch activity since 2020.</p>
    <div class="chart-container tall">
        <canvas id="launchTrendChart"></canvas>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top:1rem;">
        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Year</th><th class="number">Active Satellites</th><th class="number">Cumulative</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody id="launchTableBody">
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <div class="takeaway">
        <strong>Launch acceleration:</strong> 2025 saw the highest single-year deployment with 4,329 active satellites — nearly double the previous year. Over 90% of all active satellites were launched since 2020, reflecting the rapid industrialization of LEO.
    </div>
</div>

<!-- SECTION 5: Orbital Parameter Deep Dive -->
<div class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">5. Orbital Parameter Deep Dive</h2>
    <div class="two-col">
        <div>
            <h3 style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:0.75rem;">INCLINATION Distribution (degrees)</h3>
            <div class="chart-container">
                <canvas id="inclinationChart"></canvas>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div>
            <h3 style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:0.75rem;">MEAN_MOTION Distribution (rev/day)</h3>
            <div class="chart-container">
                <canvas id="meanMotionChart"></canvas>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
        <h3 style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Inclination vs. Mean Motion Scatter</h3>
        <div class="chart-container tall">
            <canvas id="scatterChart"></canvas>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top:1rem;">
        <h3 style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Key Orbital Parameter Statistics</h3>
        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th class="number">Min</th><th class="number">Median</th><th class="number">Max</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td>Inclination (degrees)</td><td class="number">0.00</td><td class="number">53.16</td><td class="number">150.00</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Mean Motion (rev/day)</td><td class="number">0.28</td><td class="number">15.27</td><td class="number">16.30</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Eccentricity</td><td class="number">0.00003</td><td class="number">0.00050</td><td class="number">0.8957</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- SECTION 6: Key Takeaways -->
<div class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">6. Key Takeaways & Outlook</h2>
    <div class="takeaway">
        <strong>1. Starlink dominance reshapes orbital environment:</strong> At 10,083 satellites (67.8% of total), SpaceX's Starlink is not merely the largest constellation — it is the orbital environment. Any debris, spectrum, or collision-risk policy discussion is effectively a Starlink discussion.
    </div>
    <div class="takeaway" style="border-left-color:var(--accent-orange);">
        <strong>2. LEO is overwhelmingly dominant:</strong> 86.5% of active satellites occupy LEO (MEAN_MOTION &gt; 14 rev/day), driven almost entirely by Starlink and OneWeb. MEO (9.5%) is populated primarily by navigation constellations (GPS, Galileo, GLONASS, BeiDou). GEO (3.9%) hosts traditional comsats but is the smallest regime by count.
    </div>
    <div class="takeaway" style="border-left-color:var(--accent-purple);">
        <strong>3. Launch acceleration is unprecedented:</strong> With 13,461 of 14,875 satellites (90.5%) launched since 2020, the current active fleet is overwhelmingly new. 2025 alone added 4,329 satellites — more than the entire pre-2020 operational fleet. Licensing and debris mitigation frameworks face severe stress-test timelines.
    </div>
    <div class="takeaway" style="border-left-color:var(--accent-green);">
        <strong>4. Inclination clusters at ~53° median:</strong> The median inclination of 53.16° reflects Starlink's orbital shell design (mostly 53° inclination). The concentration of traffic in this inclination band raises conjunctive event frequency and underscores need for coordination mechanisms.
    </div>
</div>

<p class="footer-note">
    Data source: CelesTrak / NORAD Two-Line Element (TLE) catalog via Kaggle (ibrahimqasimi/active-satellites-currently-in-orbit). Analysis derived entirely from data.csv. Report generated March 2026.
</p>

